    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4829" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Baebĭus</span></b> , a, um,
		adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
				name of a Roman</i> gens, e. g., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> M. Baebius, <i><span class="en">Cic. Pis.
				36, 88</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Q. Baebius Tampilus, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil.
				5, 10, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 40, 17, 8</span></i> Drak.; v. also <i><span class="en">Val. Max.
				1, 1, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 2,
				6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			G. Baebius, <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 33, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34,
			1</span></i>.—Whence, Baebia lex de praetoribus creandis,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				40, 44, 2</span></i>; cf. Fest. s. v. rogat, p. 233.</div>
